From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:22:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] DPP2: Keep the c-sign-key curve for the Configurator

Since the ppKey was added, dpp_keygen_configurator() passes conf->curve
to dpp_set_keypair() for both the c-sign-key and the ppKey.
dpp_set_keypair() sets the curve to NULL for a key on a group that the
crypto backend knows but DPP does not support. Without ppkey=, the
function then calls dpp_gen_keypair(NULL), which dereferences the NULL
curve. With OpenSSL, crypto_ec_key_group() rejects such a key before
this. The wolfSSL version of crypto_ec_key_group() maps P-192 and P-224
keys to groups 25 and 26, so these keys reach it. Reachable via
DPP_CONFIGURATOR_ADD key=<key>.

A ppKey on another curve also replaces conf->curve. The Configurator
then signs Connectors with the c-sign-key, but takes the "alg" value
and the hash function from the ppKey curve. Reachable via
DPP_CONFIGURATOR_ADD with key= and ppkey= on different curves, or with
ppkey= on a curve other than curve=.

Stop when the c-sign-key cannot be set up, before the ppKey is handled.
Reject a ppKey on a curve other than that of the c-sign-key, like
dpp_configurator_from_backup() does. The ppKey entry in Table 9 of the
DPP specification says that the ppKey "uses the same curve as the
C-sign-key".

Fixes: 9c1fbff07404 ("DPP2: Generate a privacy protection key for Configurator")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/common/dpp.c
+++ b/src/common/dpp.c
@@ -4017,6 +4017,7 @@ dpp_keygen_configurator(const char *curv
 			size_t privkey_len, const u8 *pp_key, size_t pp_key_len)
 {
 	struct dpp_configurator *conf;
+	const struct dpp_curve_params *curve_pp;
 
 	conf = os_zalloc(sizeof(*conf));
 	if (!conf)
@@ -4034,12 +4035,20 @@ dpp_keygen_configurator(const char *curv
 					      privkey_len);
 	else
 		conf->csign = dpp_gen_keypair(conf->curve);
-	if (pp_key)
-		conf->pp_key = dpp_set_keypair(&conf->curve, pp_key,
-					       pp_key_len);
-	else
+	if (!conf->csign)
+		goto fail;
+
+	if (pp_key) {
+		conf->pp_key = dpp_set_keypair(&curve_pp, pp_key, pp_key_len);
+		if (conf->pp_key && curve_pp != conf->curve) {
+			wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+				   "DPP: Mismatch in c-sign-key and ppKey groups");
+			goto fail;
+		}
+	} else {
 		conf->pp_key = dpp_gen_keypair(conf->curve);
-	if (!conf->csign || !conf->pp_key)
+	}
+	if (!conf->pp_key)
 		goto fail;
 	conf->own = 1;
 
